---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Card from "../components/Card.astro";

/* Prerendered long-form document page - see privacy.astro's docstring for
   the container/width and LAST_UPDATED reasoning; same pattern here.

   Plain-language terms for the product as it exists today - a free,
   open-source icon library. Not legal advice. */
const LAST_UPDATED = "2026-08-31";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use - Motificons"
  description="The plain-language terms for using Motificons: the site, the icon library, and the MCP server."
>
  <Header />

  <main id="main" class="pb-24">
    <div class="page-container">
      <h1 class="pt-10 text-h1 font-bold">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-meta text-ink-muted">Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

      <div class="mt-8 text-body text-ink-muted">
        <p>
          These are the terms for using Motificons - the website, the icon
          library, and the MCP server. Using any of them means you agree to
          these terms. Written in plain language on purpose; if
          anything here is unclear, email <a href="mailto:hello@motificons.app" class="prose-link">hello@motificons.app</a> before you rely on it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">The free library</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          Every icon, set and category page is free to browse and download,
          with no account and no email required. Without an account, search
          has a daily limit per visitor to keep it usable for everyone -
          browsing and downloading are not limited at all, and signing in
          removes the search limit entirely. We can adjust that limit if
          abuse patterns require it, but the library itself does not become
          paid later; free stays free.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">What an account gives you</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          Motificons is free and there is nothing to buy. An account adds
          collections, unlimited search, and an MCP key so your coding agent
          can use your icons. Everything else - every icon, every export
          format, the style engine and the Mac app - works without one.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          Use what you export in your own products, projects and client
          work, without limit on how many things you build with it. What
          these terms do not permit: reselling, redistributing or rehosting
          Motificons itself (the search tool, the MCP server, the curated
          library as a product) as a competing service. Building things that
          use icons from Motificons is exactly what it's for; building a
          copy of Motificons is not.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">Icons keep their own license</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          Nothing on this page changes what license an individual icon
          carries - every icon in the library remains under its original author's
          open-source license, whatever that license requires (some need
          visible attribution, some do not - see <a href="/licenses" class="prose-link">/licenses</a> and each
          icon's own page for the exact terms). These Terms of Use govern
          your use of Motificons the product; they do not, and cannot,
          override any upstream icon's own license. A handful of icon sets
          are third-party brand/trademark marks - a license to the artwork is
          not a trademark license, and using those still means following the
          brand's own guidelines.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">Accounts and API keys</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          You are responsible for keeping your sign-in and any API key you
          generate to yourself. An API key is shown once at creation - if it
          leaks, revoke it from your dashboard and generate a new one
          immediately; we cannot see or recover the plaintext of a key we
          have already issued (see <a href="/privacy" class="prose-link">/privacy</a>).
          The MCP server enforces a fair-use rate limit per key to keep the
          service usable for everyone; sustained automated abuse of it, or of
          the search API, is grounds for suspension.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">No warranty</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          Motificons is provided "as is." We work to keep it accurate,
          available and fast, but we make no guarantee it is free of errors,
          uninterrupted, or fit for any particular purpose. Icon metadata
          (license classification, attribution requirements) is compiled in
          good faith from upstream sources and kept as accurate as we can
          make it, but you are responsible for verifying license compliance
          for your own use, especially for commercial or trademark-sensitive
          work.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          To the extent the law allows, Motificons is not liable for indirect,
          incidental or consequential damages arising from your use of the
          site, the library, or the MCP server - including downtime, data loss, or a
          license classification later found to be wrong. Nothing here limits
          liability that cannot legally be limited (for example, in cases of
          fraud or gross negligence).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">Termination</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          We can suspend or terminate access for clear abuse - violating the
          terms above, attempting to circumvent the search limit or rate
          limits at scale, or using the service to build a
          Motificons-competing product from our data. We will always try
          email first before shutting anything down for anything short of
          active abuse.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          If these terms change materially, the date at the top of this page
          changes with them. Continuing to use Motificons after a change
          means you accept the new terms; if a change meaningfully reduces
          what an account can do, we will email affected accounts directly
          rather than rely on this page alone.
        </p>
      </div>

      <Card variant="standard" class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-h3 font-semibold">Questions</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-meta text-ink-muted">
          Email <a href="mailto:hello@motificons.app" class="prose-link">hello@motificons.app</a>
          - a person reads it, not a ticket queue.
        </p>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
